==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Erphuan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Aervanta''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Aervantex''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Like most Uber Rares, Aer must be properly protected with meatshields to be of any use, but remember that it can tank a lot of damage from [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] too. That said, Aer is screwed if a short-ranged enemy manages to get close, for it can't hit things right next to it and is prone to taking damage. In [[Cats of the Cosmos]], send Aer to back up your units, for Aer has good survivability for when it gets reached and it can contribute with decent Long Distance damage.

Aer, as a spammable sniper, bears a resemblance to [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]], with 50 less standing range, but more health.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Long Distance Barrier-Breaking attacks are Erphuan's selling point, making it an extremely consistent Barrier Breaker who may help you crush all the Barriers in a stack of enemies that may start being damaged immediately as it reaches the frontline. However, due to Erphuan's difficulty in repositioning, it is ineffective against [[UltraBaaBaa]]s who manage to enter its blind spot.

Despite its resistance, Erphuan still suffers from a blind spot, mediocre base health and only two knockbacks, which cause it to fall rather easily still, so protecting it as if it was frailer should be a top priority when using it. This set of abilities, however, open it up to being used against enemies who cannot be reached without entering their reach, as this unit would then be able to tank hits alongside the meatshields, while still being protected from enemy frontliners by said meatshields.

==='''True Form'''===
Aervanta simply gains a decent stat boost. This helps it quite a bit, making it a rather viable generalist Long Distance attacker too, with good damage, low cost, and shorter cooldown than many to make up for a lack of survivability against non-Aliens.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
As with other Ultra Forms, Aervantex gains several buffs, though these buffs come at their usual high XP and Catseyes cost, as well as several B. stones of various colors.

The first, and most important, is improved range. With a standing range increasing from 375 to 400 and its LD now hits up to 725, Aervantex can control far more of the field. Frontline enemies would have a harder time sneaking into that blindspot and backliners often find themselves within the line of fire. However, it should be noted that these increases are minimal and therefore only serve to improve existing matchups.

Second, Aervantex's survivability was improved not just by increases to standing and inner range, but also an HP increase of almost 40% for those attackers who can still get hits on it. This buff is useful for generalist survivability and especially against Aliens who can still reach Aervantex.

Finally, Aervantex can contribute much to the field with a guaranteed chance to knock any Aliens back, which combined with its already impressive reach allows it to easily gain ground against nasty Alien backliners as well.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Dodge''' can make this unit last quite a bit when it gets attacked, often allowing for others to relieve it of the enemies that are attacking it. Where it matters most, however, is against [[Cli-One]], [[Spacefish Jones]], or other foes who hit far behind their target, as Aervanta would be able to stay alive longer and contribute more. However, this talent is often luck dependent. Of course, '''Weakening''' such enemies would further improve this, making Aervanta extremely good against long ranged enemies, even without the dodge. Weaken can synergize quite well with Dodge, letting Aervanta tank more individual hits and giving it more chances to activate its Dodge ability.

Naturally, as a stat-based unit, Aervanta benefits highly from '''Health''' and '''Damage''' upgrades, which should be given to it once it is already boosted by [[Catseye]]s.

'''Resist Curse''', on the other hand, is nearly useless, as this unit does not target Relics, and would be shredded if it ever gets cursed, not to mention Curse has no effect on Barrier Breaker. It can be situationally useful, but in general isn't worth the investment.

